<title>INDIA: India approves LG Chemical investment.</title>
<headline>India approves LG Chemical investment.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian Industry Ministry said on Friday it approved a proposal by Korea's LG Chemical Ltd to establish a 100 percent subsidiary in India.</p>
<p>The ministry said in a statement that the proposal called for foreign direct investment of 3.5 billion rupees.  </p>
<p>The statement said the wholly owned subsidiary would engage &quot;either directly or through joint ventures in manufacture and distribution of diverse products which include organic and inorganic chemicals, synthetic resins, plastic and specialty chemicals&quot;.</p>
<p>- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
